{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram-, Hemolytic, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (86.67%) to BmKn2-7R or Kn2-5R-NH2 R: 33%, F: 27%, I: 20%. Activity: active against multiple clinical Salmonella strains (MIC 4-8 uM). MBC values are identical, indicating bactericidal. Showed an effect on biofilms:bacteria as well. Warning: Other bacteria not tested. In vitro toxicity: human RBC: HC50 5.6 uM, highly hemolytic. SAR: The addition of a pair of hydrophobic FF to the N-terminus made the optimized peptide highly hemolytic.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "34361810", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Molecules. 2021 Jul 31;26(15):4654. doi: 10.3390/molecules26154654. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04533", "source_id": "AP04533", "source_numeric_id": "04533", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04533", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Antimicrobial Peptide Modifications against Clinically Isolated Antibiotic-Resistant Salmonella.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
